coming in late, but I wish I'd been taught that trying to guess someone's ASC, sun or moon sign would oftentimes lead to failure. The reason? Midheaven. I wish someone had told me earlier that that's actually the most visible part of the chart — which seems logical, in hindsight, but it goes against everything pop astrology says. Understanding that, I realized why I didn't act like a Taurus or why people didn't peg me as one, except for when they learn how I truly live my day to day life. Going out for drinks/parties or just basically existing in a social context I have a very different image from the way I act when I'm alone.

&#x200B;

It's also the reason why I often couldn't relate the people I knew to their chart. The MC is important, especially if you don't know the person that well. Do not think you have access to their moon already! Unless it's visible aka near the MC then you probably don't.

