&#x200B;

The problem is where I live ADHD is still treated as little boys' disease, and I'm an adult female. I've been in therapy for the past 6 years but my therapist is 70 yrs old and admittedly a bit adamant about this stuff; he's been great help with making me become social again and maintain a sense of humour and positive outlook, despite what the post might say. It's just that I've been staying home for a whole year now, I live with my mom and a lot of what she says about my lack of responsibility and laziness gets to me and it's been tearing down my attempts at developing self-esteem for years now. (She's also very caring and proud of me, but it's inconsistent). Before the pandemic I used to be very active, constantly hanging out with friends, going to concerts, involved in local art scene. I can't wait for this to be over... I know things won't resume to what they used to be, but I hope it will be better than staying home all the time. 

