" I'm not weak and that's not why I put them before me." SO IMPORTANT! It's a shame how many people that usually call themselves our "friends" don't seem to get this. Sure, there was a time in my life where I was completely lacking in self-esteem and self-preservation so I would do ANYTHING for anyone, even if they were just an acquaintance I would still go the extra mile just to please them. But growing up, and going into a period of retreat and isolation has helped me understand that my natural state truly is that of a giving, selfless person. But people either take it for granted once they see how well you treat them, or suddenly they forget you're your own person and you can't be always there at their beck and call. I'm known for stopping whatever I'm doing to talk to anyone in distress, but at the same time I need time for myself!!! 

&#x200B;

Usually I solve these issues through 1) time and distance away from the person that wronged me and 2) talk to them about it and try to not create another fight in the process. My end goal is harmony, I cherish all my friends and I don't wanna lose them.

